777
00:52:05,415 --> 00:52:07,376
Yes. Yes, I heard it.

778
00:52:07,459 --> 00:52:08,960
Do you know what it is?

779
00:52:09,044 --> 00:52:11,088
It shows you things

780
00:52:11,171 --> 00:52:13,173
horrible things.

781
00:52:13,256 --> 00:52:14,257
What does?

782
00:52:14,341 --> 00:52:18,512
The dark inside me
from the other place.

783
00:52:18,595 --> 00:52:20,764
I won't go back there. I won't.

784
00:52:20,847 --> 00:52:22,599
No, baby bear.
Come on, open the door.

785
00:52:22,683 --> 00:52:23,725
What's happening?

786
00:52:23,809 --> 00:52:25,119
I don't think
she can talk him down.

787
00:52:25,143 --> 00:52:26,436
She'd better.

788
00:52:26,520 --> 00:52:27,789
If he opens the airlock,
he's going to turn inside out.

789
00:52:27,813 --> 00:52:29,731
Peters:
No. No, you stay with me.

790
00:52:29,815 --> 00:52:30,857
Starck: Almost got it.

791
00:52:30,941 --> 00:52:31,942
I've almost got it.

792
00:52:32,025 --> 00:52:33,360
You stay with me, Justin.

793
00:52:33,443 --> 00:52:35,028
Come on, now. Open that door!

794
00:52:35,112 --> 00:52:38,573
If you could see the things I've
seen, you wouldn't try to stop me.

795
00:52:38,657 --> 00:52:40,826
No, that's not you talking.
That's not you talking.

796
00:52:40,909 --> 00:52:42,828
That's it.
That's it, right there.

797
00:52:42,911 --> 00:52:45,288
Open the door. Go for that button.
Come on.

798
00:52:45,831 --> 00:52:48,792
Okay, okay.

799
00:52:48,875 --> 00:52:50,752
(Alarm blaring) No!

800
00:52:50,836 --> 00:52:51,920
(Screaming)

801
00:52:52,003 --> 00:52:54,339
Captain, Justin just
activated the door.

802
00:52:54,423 --> 00:52:55,799
It's on a 30-second delay.

803
00:52:55,882 --> 00:52:57,801
Miller: Justin!

804
00:53:01,680 --> 00:53:05,559
Computer voice: Stand by for
decompression in 25 seconds.

805
00:53:06,643 --> 00:53:08,603
Where am I?

806
00:53:08,687 --> 00:53:10,480
Justin: Hey.
Starck, get it fucking open!

807
00:53:10,564 --> 00:53:12,149
Hey, open the door. I can't.

808
00:53:12,232 --> 00:53:14,168
The inner door won't open when the
outside door's been triggered.

809
00:53:14,192 --> 00:53:16,027
It would decompress
the entire ship.

810
00:53:16,111 --> 00:53:19,197
Oh, my god.
Mama bear, open the door.

811
00:53:19,781 --> 00:53:21,658
Come on, please.

812
00:53:21,742 --> 00:53:22,826
Justin: Captain!

813
00:53:22,909 --> 00:53:24,202
Patch me through to him.

814
00:53:24,286 --> 00:53:26,079
Captain Miller, tell them
to open the door.

815
00:53:26,163 --> 00:53:27,914
They can't do that, Justin.

816
00:53:27,998 --> 00:53:29,458
I don't want to die in here.

817
00:53:29,541 --> 00:53:31,251
You're not gonna die.

818
00:53:31,334 --> 00:53:32,974
I want you to listen
to me very carefully,

819
00:53:33,003 --> 00:53:34,963
and I'm gonna get
you out of there.

820
00:53:38,383 --> 00:53:40,177
Oh, my god.

821
00:53:40,260 --> 00:53:43,013
It's starting. My eyes.

822
00:53:43,096 --> 00:53:44,514
Don't think about them.
Shut them.

823
00:53:44,598 --> 00:53:46,975
(Justin screaming) Just shut them as
tight as you can.

824
00:53:47,058 --> 00:53:48,226
Five seconds.

825
00:53:48,310 --> 00:53:49,537
Miller: Tuck yourself into
a crouch position.

826
00:53:49,561 --> 00:53:51,271
Make yourself into a ball now.

827
00:53:51,354 --> 00:53:54,775
Justin:
I can't breathe. Oh, god.

828
00:53:54,858 --> 00:53:57,110
Oh, god, it hurts.

829
00:53:57,194 --> 00:54:01,531
I want you to huff and puff and blow
all the air out of your lungs.

830
00:54:01,615 --> 00:54:03,551
Do you hear me? All the air out of
your lungs, Justin.

831
00:54:03,575 --> 00:54:06,161
(Screaming)

832
00:54:06,244 --> 00:54:07,454
Miller: Do it, now!

833
00:54:08,747 --> 00:54:10,499
(Justin screaming)

834
00:54:20,133 --> 00:54:21,927
Okay, baby bear.

835
00:54:23,428 --> 00:54:27,516
Got him. I got him.
Standby, people.

836
00:54:27,599 --> 00:54:29,142
Standby.

837
00:54:29,643 --> 00:54:30,977
(Justin choking)

838
00:54:31,061 --> 00:54:32,604
We've got pressure.

839
00:54:32,687 --> 00:54:34,648
Peters: We're coming, Justin. We're
coming.

840
00:54:36,233 --> 00:54:38,693
I'm going to need
five units here.

841
00:54:38,777 --> 00:54:40,362
Hold his head still.

842
00:54:40,445 --> 00:54:41,613
Peters: Okay.

843
00:54:41,696 --> 00:54:43,740
(Coughing)

844
00:54:43,824 --> 00:54:45,742
Give me some more mysoline, now.

845
00:54:45,826 --> 00:54:48,286
One thing at a time,
let's keep him breathing.

846
00:54:48,370 --> 00:54:51,370
Peters: He's bleeding out. Pressure's
still dropping. Start the drip, 15 cc.

847
00:55:00,423 --> 00:55:03,510
I've stopped the bleeding,
stabilized him best I can.

848
00:55:04,219 --> 00:55:05,345
(Sighing)

849
00:55:05,428 --> 00:55:07,347
He won't be pretty,
but he should live,

850
00:55:08,598 --> 00:55:10,600
if we make it back.
We'll make it.

851
00:55:12,769 --> 00:55:15,021
Starck, what's our time like?

852
00:55:15,105 --> 00:55:17,691
Co2 levels will become toxic in four
hours.

853
00:55:18,733 --> 00:55:20,360
All right.

854
00:55:20,443 --> 00:55:22,713
Peters, we've got to find out what
happened to the other crew

855
00:55:22,737 --> 00:55:25,615
before the same thing
happens to us.

856
00:55:25,699 --> 00:55:27,826
Well, I can work on
the log on the bridge,

857
00:55:27,909 --> 00:55:29,661
but I won't go back to medical.

858
00:55:29,744 --> 00:55:30,871
Fine.

859
00:55:31,830 --> 00:55:33,039
Yes, sir.

860
00:55:34,958 --> 00:55:37,043
Justin said something about

861
00:55:38,545 --> 00:55:40,422
"the dark inside me."

862
00:55:41,631 --> 00:55:42,757
What's that mean?

863
00:55:43,800 --> 00:55:44,801
Doctor?

864
00:55:47,637 --> 00:55:49,806
I don't think it means anything.

865
00:55:54,394 --> 00:55:56,938
Miller: Don't you walk away
from me, mister.

866
00:55:58,899 --> 00:56:00,567
I'd like some answers, doctor.

867
00:56:00,650 --> 00:56:03,194
I'd like to know why one of my men
tried to commit suicide

868
00:56:03,278 --> 00:56:04,755
by throwing himself
out of an airlock.

869
00:56:04,779 --> 00:56:06,489
I'd like to know
what caused that noise.

870
00:56:06,573 --> 00:56:09,117
Look, thermal changes
in the hull

871
00:56:09,200 --> 00:56:12,495
could've caused the metal to expand
and contract rapidly

872
00:56:12,579 --> 00:56:14,179
causing reverberations.
This is possible.

873
00:56:14,205 --> 00:56:16,416
Bullshit! You built
this fucking ship.

874
00:56:16,499 --> 00:56:18,293
You've given me
nothing but bullshit.

875
00:56:18,376 --> 00:56:20,754
What do you want me to say?

876
00:56:20,837 --> 00:56:24,674
You said the ship's drive creates a
gateway.

877
00:56:24,758 --> 00:56:26,426
Yeah. To what?

878
00:56:27,761 --> 00:56:29,638
I don't know. Where did it go?

879
00:56:29,721 --> 00:56:32,724
Where did you send it?
I don't know.

880
00:56:32,807 --> 00:56:34,893
Where has it been for the last seven
years?

881
00:56:34,976 --> 00:56:36,478
Look, I don't know.

882
00:56:36,561 --> 00:56:38,563
"I don't know," is not good enough,
doctor.

883
00:56:38,647 --> 00:56:40,482
You're supposed to be
the fucking expert.

884
00:56:40,565 --> 00:56:42,734
I need answers. That's your job.

885
00:56:42,817 --> 00:56:44,569
Now, the other place,
where is that?

886
00:56:44,653 --> 00:56:47,238
I don't know! I don't know!

887
00:56:47,322 --> 00:56:49,282
Look,

888
00:56:49,366 --> 00:56:52,577
there's a lot of things happening
around here that I don't fully understand.

889
00:56:52,661 --> 00:56:54,412
(Stuttering) I need time.

890
00:56:56,247 --> 00:56:57,958
I see.

891
00:56:58,041 --> 00:57:00,794
Well, that's exactly
what we don't have, doctor.

892
00:57:06,508 --> 00:57:08,051
Corrick: Captain!

893
00:57:14,057 --> 00:57:15,558
Don't leave me!

894
00:57:22,065 --> 00:57:23,650
Don't leave me!

895
00:57:29,197 --> 00:57:30,281
Please!

896
00:57:33,743 --> 00:57:37,539
For god's sakes, help me!

897
00:57:44,546 --> 00:57:45,964
(Exhales)

898
00:57:47,716 --> 00:57:49,092
It's in your head.

899
00:57:52,053 --> 00:57:53,555
It's just in your head.

900
00:58:13,867 --> 00:58:15,243
God help us.

901
00:58:16,911 --> 00:58:18,913
(Thunder rumbling)

902
00:58:21,082 --> 00:58:23,460
Miller: I'm telling you,
it was his voice I heard.

903
00:58:23,543 --> 00:58:24,794
He was calling to me.

904
00:58:24,878 --> 00:58:27,130
A young bosun
named Eddie corrick.

905
00:58:29,174 --> 00:58:31,092
We served on
the Goliath together.

906
00:58:33,094 --> 00:58:37,307
When the O2 tanks ruptured, four of
us made it to the lifeboat.

907
00:58:37,390 --> 00:58:38,993
But corrick was still
on board the Goliath

908
00:58:39,017 --> 00:58:40,685
when the fire broke out.

909
00:58:42,103 --> 00:58:44,606
You ever seen
fire in zero gravity?

910
00:58:46,733 --> 00:58:48,109
It's beautiful.

911
00:58:50,403 --> 00:58:51,946
It's like liquid.

912
00:58:53,198 --> 00:58:55,450
It slides all over everything.

913
00:58:56,701 --> 00:58:58,119
Comes up in waves.

914
00:58:59,996 --> 00:59:01,915
And they just kept hitting him,

915
00:59:02,916 --> 00:59:04,501
wave after wave.

916
00:59:06,795 --> 00:59:09,005
He was screaming
for me to save him.

917
00:59:10,507 --> 00:59:11,716
What did you do?

918
00:59:12,592 --> 00:59:14,427
I did the only thing I could.

919
00:59:16,930 --> 00:59:20,141
I closed the lifeboat hatch,
and I left him behind.

920
00:59:24,395 --> 00:59:26,856
I swore I'd never
lose another man.

921
00:59:28,399 --> 00:59:30,819
I've known you a long time.

922
00:59:30,902 --> 00:59:32,070
You never told me that.

923
00:59:32,153 --> 00:59:35,115
That's just it, d.J.,
I... I never told anybody.

924
00:59:36,699 --> 00:59:39,702
But this ship knew about it.

925
00:59:39,786 --> 00:59:43,123
It knows my fears.
It knows my secrets.

926
00:59:44,582 --> 00:59:47,293
Gets inside your head,
and it shows you.

927
00:59:48,837 --> 00:59:50,547
I wasn't going to tell you this.

928
00:59:53,216 --> 00:59:55,552
I've been listening
to the distress signal.

929
00:59:56,427 --> 00:59:57,887
And I, um...

930
01:00:00,014 --> 01:00:02,934
I think I made a mistake
in the translation.

931
01:00:03,810 --> 01:00:05,854
(Man speaking indistinctly)

932
01:00:09,357 --> 01:00:10,483
(Sighs)

933
01:00:11,776 --> 01:00:12,944
Go on.

934
01:00:14,445 --> 01:00:16,614
I thought it said "liberate me."

935
01:00:17,407 --> 01:00:18,658
"Save me."

936
01:00:20,076 --> 01:00:21,578
But it's not "me."

937
01:00:22,871 --> 01:00:25,498
It's "liberate tutume."

938
01:00:26,291 --> 01:00:27,292
"Save yourself."

939
01:00:28,793 --> 01:00:29,836
And it gets worse.

940
01:00:30,795 --> 01:00:32,630
(Man speaking indistinctly)

941
01:00:34,257 --> 01:00:35,425
There.

942
01:00:36,759 --> 01:00:37,844
I think

943
01:00:38,928 --> 01:00:41,973
that says "ex inferis."

944
01:00:43,558 --> 01:00:45,143
"Save yourself

945
01:00:47,645 --> 01:00:48,688
"from hell."

946
01:00:50,607 --> 01:00:55,403
Look, if what
Dr. Weir tells us is true,

947
01:00:55,486 --> 01:00:58,448
this ship has been beyond the
boundaries of our universe,

948
01:00:59,449 --> 01:01:01,618
of known scientific reality.

949
01:01:03,077 --> 01:01:04,913
Who knows where it's been,

950
01:01:05,788 --> 01:01:07,207
what it's seen,

951
01:01:09,417 --> 01:01:11,544
and what
it's brought back with it?

952
01:01:12,337 --> 01:01:13,630
From hell.

953
01:01:17,926 --> 01:01:20,094
You don't believe in
that kind of stuff, do you?

954
01:01:23,932 --> 01:01:27,518
Whoever sent that message,
he sure believes in hell.

955
01:01:28,353 --> 01:01:29,854
Cooper: Captain Miller.

956
01:01:34,525 --> 01:01:36,194
Whatever it is, Coop,
it better be good.

957
01:01:36,277 --> 01:01:37,737
Cooper: Yes, sir.

958
01:01:37,820 --> 01:01:40,216
Ready to repressurize the Clark and
get the hell out of here.

959
01:01:40,240 --> 01:01:41,574
On my way.

960
01:01:46,412 --> 01:01:48,456
Miller: Come on, baby,
don't let me down.

961
01:01:56,339 --> 01:01:59,217
Hello, baby. Papa's home.

962
01:02:00,009 --> 01:02:01,386
Smith: She's holding.

963
01:02:02,637 --> 01:02:04,013
Oh, shit.

964
01:02:04,097 --> 01:02:06,933
Cooper: Skipper, we're still venting
trace gasses.

965
01:02:07,016 --> 01:02:08,935
Give me about 20 minutes
to plug the hole.

966
01:02:09,018 --> 01:02:11,896
Miller: Cooper,
you are the lifesaver.

967
01:02:11,980 --> 01:02:14,148
20 minutes and we're underway.

968
01:02:17,652 --> 01:02:18,736
Shit.

969
01:02:22,198 --> 01:02:23,908
Got any coffee?

970
01:02:23,992 --> 01:02:25,868
Yeah, but it's cold.

971
01:02:25,952 --> 01:02:27,120
Great.

972
01:02:36,129 --> 01:02:37,463
(People screaming)

973
01:02:37,547 --> 01:02:38,673
Starck.

974
01:02:44,304 --> 01:02:45,763
Miller?

975
01:02:45,847 --> 01:02:47,724
(Woman screaming)

976
01:02:50,643 --> 01:02:52,812
(People screaming)

977
01:02:54,063 --> 01:02:55,148
(Speaking Latin)

978
01:03:06,326 --> 01:03:07,535
We're leaving.

979
01:03:10,830 --> 01:03:12,582
No, we can't leave.

980
01:03:13,916 --> 01:03:15,626
Our orders are specific.

981
01:03:15,710 --> 01:03:18,504
Rescue the crew, salvage what's left
of the ship.

982
01:03:18,588 --> 01:03:20,298
The crew is dead, doctor.

983
01:03:20,381 --> 01:03:21,382
Your ship killed them.

984
01:03:21,466 --> 01:03:23,009
We came here to do a job.

985
01:03:23,092 --> 01:03:25,553
We're aborting, doctor!

986
01:03:25,636 --> 01:03:28,890
Starck, download the files from the
event horizon's computers.

987
01:03:28,973 --> 01:03:30,975
D.j., I want you to get Justin

988
01:03:31,059 --> 01:03:32,536
prepped and ready to move him back to
the Clark.

989
01:03:32,560 --> 01:03:34,270
There's stuff I wanna
get from medical.

990
01:03:34,354 --> 01:03:36,856
We'd better move him in the tank. No
problem. Do it.

991
01:03:38,816 --> 01:03:40,193
Peters. Yes, sir.

992
01:03:40,276 --> 01:03:42,046
I want you to get the co2 scrubbers
back into the Clark.

993
01:03:42,070 --> 01:03:44,405
Take smitty with you. Right.

994
01:03:44,489 --> 01:03:45,740
Weir: Captain.

995
01:03:47,450 --> 01:03:48,826
Captain.

996
01:03:51,079 --> 01:03:52,246
Don't do this.

997
01:03:53,122 --> 01:03:54,332
It's done.

998
01:03:56,209 --> 01:03:58,044
What about my ship?
You can't just leave her.

999
01:03:58,127 --> 01:03:59,807
I have no intention of
leaving her, doctor.

1000
01:03:59,879 --> 01:04:01,881
I will take the Lewis & Clark
to a safe distance

1001
01:04:01,964 --> 01:04:04,258
and then I will launch tac missiles
at the event horizon

1002
01:04:04,342 --> 01:04:07,053
until I'm satisfied she's vaporized.
Fuck this ship.

1003
01:04:07,136 --> 01:04:08,471
(Grunting)

1004
01:04:14,102 --> 01:04:15,853
(Alarm beeping)

1005
01:04:15,937 --> 01:04:18,815
Captain Miller, the bio—scan just
went off the scale.

1006
01:04:18,898 --> 01:04:20,691
It looks like the core

1007
01:04:20,775 --> 01:04:23,194
is draining power
from the rest of the ship.

1008
01:04:23,277 --> 01:04:24,779
Get the files. Vacate.

1009
01:04:24,862 --> 01:04:26,239
I want off this ship.

1010
01:04:26,322 --> 01:04:30,034
You can't leave.
She won't let you.

1011
01:04:30,118 --> 01:04:32,638
You just get your gear and get back
on the Lewis & Clark, doctor

1012
01:04:32,703 --> 01:04:34,580
or you'll find
yourself walkin' home.

1013
01:04:34,664 --> 01:04:36,165
I am home.

1014
01:04:37,125 --> 01:04:38,918
Peters: Let's go!

1015
01:04:39,001 --> 01:04:40,211
Ready?

1016
01:04:41,587 --> 01:04:42,713
D.j.: Shot.

1017
01:04:43,798 --> 01:04:45,133
Peters: Come on. Come on.

1018
01:04:46,259 --> 01:04:47,718
Ready? Shot.

1019
01:04:53,057 --> 01:04:55,101
Shot. Okay.

1020
01:04:55,184 --> 01:04:57,395
Peters, can we go? This place is
really freaking me out.

1021
01:04:57,478 --> 01:04:58,997
Yeah, you wanna breathe
on the way home.

1022
01:04:59,021 --> 01:05:00,398
No, I don't! Let's go!

1023
01:05:00,481 --> 01:05:01,858
Shit!

1024
01:05:01,941 --> 01:05:03,317
25. Come on!

1025
01:05:03,401 --> 01:05:04,986
We need 25. Peters!

1026
01:05:05,486 --> 01:05:07,530
Come on! Got it!

1027
01:05:21,377 --> 01:05:22,879
(Banging)

1028
01:05:24,672 --> 01:05:26,424
(Banging continues)

1029
01:06:22,772 --> 01:06:24,273
(Panting)

1030
01:06:47,922 --> 01:06:49,715
(Screaming)

1031
01:07:32,425 --> 01:07:34,260
Oh, no. Peters.

1032
01:07:40,433 --> 01:07:41,934
Oh, god.

1033
01:07:47,982 --> 01:07:49,483
Claire: Billy.

1034
01:07:59,160 --> 01:08:00,328
Claire?

1035
01:08:07,710 --> 01:08:08,878
Claire.

1036
01:08:10,630 --> 01:08:12,214
It's me. I'm home.

1037
01:08:14,800 --> 01:08:16,260
I'm home.

1038
01:08:20,264 --> 01:08:24,018
I know I wasn't there
when you needed me,

1039
01:08:24,101 --> 01:08:26,062
and I'm sorry I...

1040
01:08:26,896 --> 01:08:30,316
I let my work come between us.

1041
01:08:34,278 --> 01:08:37,031
God, Claire, no.

1042
01:08:37,114 --> 01:08:40,076
I'm begging you, please.
Please, don't.

1043
01:08:41,118 --> 01:08:43,579
Not again, please.

1044
01:08:43,663 --> 01:08:45,665
I've been so...

1045
01:08:50,503 --> 01:08:52,505
I've been so...

1046
01:08:54,465 --> 01:08:55,716
Claire: Billy.

1047
01:08:57,134 --> 01:08:58,511
It's all right.

1048
01:09:01,639 --> 01:09:03,182
I've been so alone.

1049
01:09:03,265 --> 01:09:05,059
You'll never be alone again.

1050
01:09:06,811 --> 01:09:11,399
You're with me now.
You're with me

1051
01:09:11,482 --> 01:09:15,319
and I have such wonderful,
wonderful things

1052
01:09:16,570 --> 01:09:17,780
to show you.

1053
01:09:21,117 --> 01:09:22,743
(Screaming)

1054
01:09:36,882 --> 01:09:38,300
Damn, I'm good.

1055
01:09:41,721 --> 01:09:43,097
Coop.

1056
01:09:43,180 --> 01:09:45,057
Coop, how long
are you going to take?

1057
01:09:45,141 --> 01:09:46,827
'Cause I've got to get
the hell out of here.

1058
01:09:46,851 --> 01:09:49,437
Look, you can kiss my ass, Smith,
'cause I'm done.

1059
01:09:49,520 --> 01:09:51,772
Just give me a second
to collect my tools

1060
01:09:51,856 --> 01:09:53,190
and we can get out of dodge.

1061
01:09:53,274 --> 01:09:54,567
Two minutes tops.

1062
01:09:54,650 --> 01:09:55,735
Roger that.

1063
01:09:55,818 --> 01:09:56,986
(Banging)

1064
01:10:01,657 --> 01:10:03,033
Smith: Weir.

1065
01:10:03,117 --> 01:10:05,035
Dr. Weir.

1066
01:10:05,119 --> 01:10:06,245
Weir!

1067
01:10:09,331 --> 01:10:10,374
Weir!

1068
01:10:12,585 --> 01:10:14,795
Dr. Weir, get your ass
back on board now!

1069
01:10:14,879 --> 01:10:15,921
Weir!

1070
01:10:17,381 --> 01:10:19,300
Shit.

1071
01:10:19,383 --> 01:10:21,552
Captain Miller, captain Miller, do
you copy? Over.

1072
01:10:21,635 --> 01:10:24,263
Captain Miller. Captain Miller, do
you copy? Over.

1073
01:10:24,346 --> 01:10:25,765
Go ahead, smitty.

1074
01:10:25,848 --> 01:10:27,928
I've just seen Weir messing around on
the Clark, sir.

1075
01:10:30,686 --> 01:10:33,189
Standby, smitty,
I wanna check something out.

1076
01:10:38,736 --> 01:10:39,945
Smith, get out of there.

1077
01:10:40,029 --> 01:10:41,447
Come again, sir?

1078
01:10:41,530 --> 01:10:43,341
One of the explosives
is missing from the corridor.

1079
01:10:43,365 --> 01:10:44,676
Weir might have
put it on the Clark.

1080
01:10:44,700 --> 01:10:45,785
No. No way.

1081
01:10:45,868 --> 01:10:47,161
No, no, sir, no way.

1082
01:10:47,244 --> 01:10:48,472
I've just put it
back together, sir.

1083
01:10:48,496 --> 01:10:49,997
Get off the Clark now, Smith!

1084
01:11:00,049 --> 01:11:02,009
Where the fucking hell are you?

1085
01:11:24,782 --> 01:11:26,367
Got you.

1086
01:11:26,450 --> 01:11:28,077
Miller: Hang on, smitty.
I'm coming!

1087
01:11:32,373 --> 01:11:34,083
(Beeping)

1088
01:11:35,501 --> 01:11:36,961
(Shuddering)

1089
01:11:42,258 --> 01:11:43,425
No!

1090
01:11:50,307 --> 01:11:51,600
Shit!

1091
01:12:34,310 --> 01:12:35,769
Cooper: Shit!

1092
01:12:35,853 --> 01:12:37,229
Where the fuck am I going?

1093
01:12:37,313 --> 01:12:39,106
Why does this shit
got to happen to me?

1094
01:12:39,189 --> 01:12:40,357
Fuck.

1095
01:12:42,610 --> 01:12:44,486
All right, think, Coop.
Think. Think.

1096
01:12:44,570 --> 01:12:46,780
All right, all right, I got to get
back to the ship.

1097
01:12:46,864 --> 01:12:48,782
I got to get back to the ship, all
right.

1098
01:12:48,866 --> 01:12:50,034
I gotta blow my air tank.

1099
01:12:50,826 --> 01:12:52,161
I'll blow my air tank.

1100
01:12:52,244 --> 01:12:54,079
(Hissing)

1101
01:12:54,163 --> 01:12:55,539
All right. Fuck.

1102
01:12:55,623 --> 01:12:57,666
This better work.
This shit better work.

1103
01:12:57,750 --> 01:12:59,919
All right. Here I go. All right.

1104
01:13:00,002 --> 01:13:01,712
(Beeping)
One, two, three. Come on.

1105
01:13:01,795 --> 01:13:04,048
Come on, come on, come on.

1106
01:13:04,131 --> 01:13:06,800
Yes! Yes! Yes!

1107
01:13:07,676 --> 01:13:10,054
Here I come, motherfuckers!

1108
01:13:17,061 --> 01:13:18,103
D.j.

1109
01:13:19,355 --> 01:13:20,356
What was that?

1110
01:13:20,439 --> 01:13:21,649
Clark's gone.

1111
01:13:22,524 --> 01:13:24,109
Smitty and Cooper are dead.

1112
01:13:24,193 --> 01:13:25,569
What? What the...

1113
01:13:25,653 --> 01:13:27,780
It was Weir. You spot him, you take
him out.

1114
01:13:28,739 --> 01:13:29,740
Understood.

1115
01:13:30,866 --> 01:13:31,867
Be careful, d.J.

1116
01:13:32,618 --> 01:13:33,994
Don't worry about Weir.

1117
01:13:34,870 --> 01:13:35,871
I'll take care of him.

1118
01:13:43,212 --> 01:13:44,546
(Choking)

1119
01:13:46,340 --> 01:13:47,549
D.j.?

1120
01:13:49,051 --> 01:13:50,302
(Grunting)

1121
01:13:58,227 --> 01:14:00,145
(Screaming)

1122
01:14:00,229 --> 01:14:03,732
Miller: D.J.? D.J., answer me!

1123
01:14:15,619 --> 01:14:16,662
(Knife cutting)

1124
01:14:16,745 --> 01:14:18,038
(Groaning)

1125
01:14:51,655 --> 01:14:52,990
Miller: Okay, Dr. Weir.

1126
01:14:58,078 --> 01:15:01,415
(Cocking gun) You don't wanna leave
your ship?

1127
01:15:01,498 --> 01:15:03,042
You never will.

1128
01:15:54,051 --> 01:15:55,928
(Thunder clapping)

1129
01:16:02,184 --> 01:16:03,352
Starck.

1130
01:16:25,707 --> 01:16:27,000
It's okay.

1131
01:16:31,255 --> 01:16:33,298
I'm gonna get you out of here.

1132
01:16:36,385 --> 01:16:37,553
Okay.

1133
01:16:41,932 --> 01:16:43,183
Easy.

1134
01:16:58,574 --> 01:17:00,742
Oh, my god.

1135
01:17:02,411 --> 01:17:04,371
What happened to your eyes?

1136
01:17:04,454 --> 01:17:08,417
Where we're going,
we won't need eyes to see.

1137
01:17:08,500 --> 01:17:10,502
What are you talking about?

1138
01:17:10,586 --> 01:17:15,215
I created the event horizon
to reach the stars.

1139
01:17:15,299 --> 01:17:18,719
But she's gone
much, much farther than that.

1140
01:17:19,970 --> 01:17:22,431
She tore a hole in our universe,

1141
01:17:22,514 --> 01:17:25,642
a gateway to another dimension.

1142
01:17:26,768 --> 01:17:29,104
A dimension of pure chaos,

1143
01:17:29,980 --> 01:17:32,858
pure evil.

1144
01:17:32,941 --> 01:17:36,153
When she crossed over,
she was just a ship.

1145
01:17:36,236 --> 01:17:38,530
But when she came back,

1146
01:17:39,615 --> 01:17:42,034
she was alive.

1147
01:17:43,327 --> 01:17:45,078
Look at her, Miller.

1148
01:17:46,455 --> 01:17:49,541
Isn't she beautiful?

1149
01:17:49,625 --> 01:17:53,420
Your beautiful ship
killed its crew, doctor.

1150
01:17:54,838 --> 01:17:56,215
Well,

1151
01:17:57,841 --> 01:18:00,093
now she has another crew.

1152
01:18:02,054 --> 01:18:04,014
Now she has us.

1153
01:18:11,313 --> 01:18:12,898
What do you think
you're doing, doctor?

1154
01:18:14,358 --> 01:18:16,818
You wanted to know
where the ship has been,

1155
01:18:17,819 --> 01:18:19,947
so now you'll find out.

1156
01:18:23,450 --> 01:18:24,701
(Grunting)

1157
01:18:33,835 --> 01:18:35,315
If you miss me,
you blow out the hull.

1158
01:18:36,213 --> 01:18:37,756
What makes you think I'll miss?

1159
01:18:39,925 --> 01:18:41,593
Cooper: That's right, I'm back!

1160
01:18:41,677 --> 01:18:44,221
I'm... oh, shit,
I can't stop. Hey!

1161
01:18:44,304 --> 01:18:46,139
Hey! Fuck.

1162
01:18:46,598 --> 01:18:48,392
(Grunting)

1163
01:18:48,475 --> 01:18:51,311
What? Who the fuck? Oh, shit!

1164
01:18:53,063 --> 01:18:54,064
(Screaming)

1165
01:19:24,845 --> 01:19:26,680
(Yelling)

1166
01:19:26,763 --> 01:19:27,889
Miller!

1167
01:19:30,392 --> 01:19:31,393
(Grunting)

1168
01:19:33,395 --> 01:19:35,105
(Weir screaming)

1169
01:20:26,406 --> 01:20:29,034
Miller! Miller!

1170
01:20:32,621 --> 01:20:34,081
(Alarm blaring)

1171
01:20:42,339 --> 01:20:43,799
Give me your hand!

1172
01:20:44,591 --> 01:20:45,592
(Grunting)

1173
01:20:52,432 --> 01:20:53,433
Miller: Come on!

1174
01:20:54,101 --> 01:20:55,268
I can't!

1175
01:20:57,145 --> 01:20:58,855
I'm not leaving you.

1176
01:21:16,873 --> 01:21:17,916
(Alarm blaring)

1177
01:21:19,000 --> 01:21:20,585
Fonnard airlock.

1178
01:21:26,133 --> 01:21:27,551
It can't be Weir.

1179
01:21:28,760 --> 01:21:30,846
I'm not taking any chances.

1180
01:21:31,513 --> 01:21:32,597
You watch your back.

1181
01:21:44,151 --> 01:21:45,151
Yo! Don't hit me.

1182
01:21:45,193 --> 01:21:46,445
Starck: Cooper!

1183
01:21:46,653 --> 01:21:48,447
Take it off! Take it off!

1184
01:21:50,365 --> 01:21:51,992
I can't breathe.
I can't breathe.

1185
01:21:52,075 --> 01:21:54,619
You're okay. You're okay.
It's over.

1186
01:21:54,703 --> 01:21:56,663
No, it's not.

1187
01:21:56,746 --> 01:21:58,123
Weir's activated
the gravity drive.

1188
01:21:58,206 --> 01:21:59,458
We gotta shut it down.

1189
01:21:59,541 --> 01:22:01,626
How? The bridge is gone.
What about engineering?

1190
01:22:01,710 --> 01:22:03,062
You think you can shut it down from
there?

1191
01:22:03,086 --> 01:22:05,422
I don't know the process.
Dr. Weir was the expert.

1192
01:22:05,505 --> 01:22:07,358
I don't want to go where the other
crew went, okay?

1193
01:22:07,382 --> 01:22:08,800
I'd rather be dead.

1194
01:22:08,884 --> 01:22:10,302
Okay. Okay, we blow
the fucker up.

1195
01:22:10,385 --> 01:22:11,386
We blow it up?

1196
01:22:11,470 --> 01:22:15,265
Do like Weir said.
Blow the corridor,

1197
01:22:15,348 --> 01:22:17,809
separate us from
the rest of ship.

1198
01:22:17,893 --> 01:22:19,644
Use the foredecks as a lifeboat.

1199
01:22:19,728 --> 01:22:21,980
With any luck, tdrs will pick up our
emergency beacon.

1200
01:22:22,063 --> 01:22:24,191
We prep the gravity couches,
put ourselves in stasis

1201
01:22:24,274 --> 01:22:26,151
and standby for
a search and rescue team.

1202
01:22:26,234 --> 01:22:28,695
Meantime, I'm gonna go manually arm
these explosives.

1203
01:22:28,778 --> 01:22:30,405
Skipper, will this shit work?

1204
01:22:30,489 --> 01:22:32,467
It worked for Dr. Weir. You go
activate the emergency beacon.

1205
01:22:32,491 --> 01:22:33,593
You get back here double-quick.

1206
01:22:33,617 --> 01:22:35,076
Yes, sir. I'll come with you.

1207
01:22:35,160 --> 01:22:37,204
You stay here. You prep the gravity
couches.

1208
01:22:37,287 --> 01:22:38,288
Miller.

1209
01:22:40,874 --> 01:22:42,354
Close this door
behind me, lieutenant.

1210
01:22:52,886 --> 01:22:56,848
Computer voice: Gateway opening in t
minus five minutes.

1211
01:23:03,313 --> 01:23:05,982
Emergency beacon activated.

1212
01:23:07,609 --> 01:23:08,610
Yes.

1213
01:23:09,611 --> 01:23:10,862
Blood?

1214
01:23:18,328 --> 01:23:19,496
Oh, fuck me.

1215
01:23:20,580 --> 01:23:21,957
Fuck me.

1216
01:23:22,958 --> 01:23:24,042
Starck!

1217
01:23:34,553 --> 01:23:35,554
(Screaming)

1218
01:23:47,857 --> 01:23:48,858
Starck!

1219
01:23:53,321 --> 01:23:54,614
Run!

1220
01:23:57,367 --> 01:24:01,705
Computer voice: Gateway opening in t
minus three minutes.

1221
01:24:05,667 --> 01:24:08,378
Detonator release is authorized.

1222
01:24:09,629 --> 01:24:12,591
The main corridor is now armed.

1223
01:24:12,674 --> 01:24:15,051
We're armed.
She's ready to blow.

1224
01:24:15,135 --> 01:24:18,471
I repeat, we are armed.
She's ready to blow.

1225
01:24:18,555 --> 01:24:20,890
Miller. Miller, can you hear me?

1226
01:24:20,974 --> 01:24:23,059
We have to get out of here now.

1227
01:24:23,143 --> 01:24:24,311
(Fire rumbling)

1228
01:24:25,687 --> 01:24:27,105
You let me burn.

1229
01:24:45,081 --> 01:24:49,628
Computer voice: Gateway opening in t
minus two minutes.

1230
01:25:06,269 --> 01:25:07,437
Corrick: Miller.

1231
01:25:08,855 --> 01:25:09,981
(Miller screaming)

1232
01:25:25,246 --> 01:25:26,665
(Miller coughing)

1233
01:25:26,748 --> 01:25:28,625
Corrick: You left me behind.

1234
01:25:31,086 --> 01:25:32,504
No, you're not Edmund corrick.

1235
01:25:32,587 --> 01:25:33,713
I watched him die.

1236
01:25:38,551 --> 01:25:39,844
Weir?

1237
01:25:39,928 --> 01:25:42,347
(Chuckung)

1238
01:25:42,430 --> 01:25:44,516
The ship brought me back.

1239
01:25:44,599 --> 01:25:46,518
I told you
she won't let me leave.

1240
01:25:46,601 --> 01:25:48,687
She won't let anyoneleave.

1241
01:25:48,770 --> 01:25:52,023
Did you really think
you could destroy this ship?

1242
01:25:52,107 --> 01:25:55,568
She's defied space and time.

1243
01:25:55,652 --> 01:25:58,780
She's been to a place you couldn't
possibly imagine.

1244
01:25:59,280 --> 01:26:00,448
And now

1245
01:26:01,449 --> 01:26:03,535
it is time to go back.

1246
01:26:03,618 --> 01:26:05,704
I know, to hell.

1247
01:26:05,787 --> 01:26:09,666
You know nothing.
Hell is only a word.

1248
01:26:09,749 --> 01:26:13,878
The reality is much, much worse.

1249
01:26:16,631 --> 01:26:19,134
Now let me show you.

1250
01:26:21,010 --> 01:26:22,220
Help me!

1251
01:26:23,763 --> 01:26:25,557
(Screaming)

1252
01:26:25,640 --> 01:26:27,392
No!

1253
01:26:29,519 --> 01:26:31,229
No.

1254
01:26:31,312 --> 01:26:33,064
You see?

1255
01:26:33,148 --> 01:26:36,735
They're not dead.
They're not dead.

1256
01:26:36,818 --> 01:26:37,986
Not yet.

1257
01:26:38,069 --> 01:26:40,321
(Yelling)

1258
01:26:40,405 --> 01:26:41,948
You won't

1259
01:26:42,031 --> 01:26:46,077
take my crew.

1260
01:26:46,161 --> 01:26:48,079
(Screaming)

1261
01:26:52,917 --> 01:26:53,918
(Miller grunting)

1262
01:27:05,054 --> 01:27:06,931
They're not your crew anymore.

1263
01:27:07,015 --> 01:27:08,933
They belong to the ship.

1264
01:27:09,017 --> 01:27:10,393
Computer voice: Gateway opening.

1265
01:27:13,813 --> 01:27:15,273
(Groaning)

1266
01:27:23,364 --> 01:27:24,365
(Screams)

1267
01:27:25,325 --> 01:27:26,451
Miller: Take me.

1268
01:27:27,702 --> 01:27:29,412
You take me.
You leave them alone.

1269
01:27:29,496 --> 01:27:32,957
No. There is no escape.

1270
01:27:35,335 --> 01:27:37,170
The gateway is open

1271
01:27:37,253 --> 01:27:40,131
and you are all coming with me.

1272
01:27:44,886 --> 01:27:46,095
Do you see?

1273
01:27:50,850 --> 01:27:52,143
Do you see?

1274
01:27:54,854 --> 01:27:56,147
Do you see?

1275
01:27:58,900 --> 01:28:00,151
Yes,

1276
01:28:01,611 --> 01:28:03,029
I see.

1277
01:28:06,741 --> 01:28:08,076
No!

1278
01:28:56,708 --> 01:28:58,209
(Explosion)

1279
01:29:29,240 --> 01:29:30,241
Miller.

1280
01:29:37,749 --> 01:29:40,585
Man: This is rescue one. We have
contact.

1281
01:29:42,295 --> 01:29:44,923
Approaching the wreckage
of the event horizon.

1282
01:29:45,757 --> 01:29:47,258
Prepare to board.

1283
01:29:56,935 --> 01:29:59,896
I'm entering the grav couch bay.

1284
01:29:59,979 --> 01:30:03,399
It doesn't appear to have been
damaged in the explosion.

1285
01:30:05,526 --> 01:30:08,071
There appear to be
three survivors,

1286
01:30:08,154 --> 01:30:12,116
Cooper, Justin,
lieutenant starck.

1287
01:30:12,200 --> 01:30:15,119
Justin seems to have suffered
massive injuries

1288
01:30:15,203 --> 01:30:16,871
but he's still alive.

1289
01:30:18,873 --> 01:30:20,833
The grav couches
still have power.

1290
01:30:23,962 --> 01:30:26,130
I'm opening the first tank now.

1291
01:30:30,843 --> 01:30:32,220
(Gasping)

1292
01:30:36,349 --> 01:30:38,267
It's all right. It's okay.

1293
01:30:38,351 --> 01:30:39,352
You're safe now.

1294
01:30:39,435 --> 01:30:40,687
Justin, Cooper.

1295
01:30:40,770 --> 01:30:42,897
They're fine. They're with us.

1296
01:30:44,190 --> 01:30:45,316
They're with us.

1297
01:30:45,400 --> 01:30:46,818
(Screaming)

1298
01:30:48,736 --> 01:30:50,321
Cooper: Starck. Starck.

1299
01:30:50,405 --> 01:30:51,698
Stay calm. It's all right.

1300
01:30:51,781 --> 01:30:52,824
Calm down, it's me.

1301
01:30:52,907 --> 01:30:53,908
Breathe deeply.

1302
01:30:53,992 --> 01:30:55,326
Starck. Breathe deeply.

1303
01:30:55,410 --> 01:30:57,495
It's the rescue team.
